      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(agents): handle stdout/stderr stream errors in find tool",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe `find` tool spawns `fd`/`find` and reads stdout/stderr through a `readline` interface. If either stream emits an error before or during line processing, the error is not handled, which can crash the agent process with an unhandled exception.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nMirror the fix already applied to `bash` (#101005) and `grep` (#101014): attach explicit error handlers to both the readline interface and the raw stdout/stderr streams so transient stream errors are logged and the tool result reflects the failure instead of propagating an unhandled exception.\n\n## User Impact\n\nAgent runs using the `find` tool are more resilient to OS-level stream failures (e.g., pipe errors, resource limits).\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Added regression tests in `src/agents/sessions/tools/find.fd.test.ts` covering both stdout and stderr stream errors.\n- Added a real behavior proof script at `scripts/proof/find-tool-stream-errors.mts` that spawns the tool and forces a stream error, verifying the process does not crash.\n- Local run:\n  - `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/sessions/tools/find.fd.test.ts` passed\n  - `OPENCLAW_OXLINT_SKIP_PREPARE=1 node scripts/run-oxlint.mjs src/agents/sessions/tools/find.ts src/agents/sessions/tools/find.fd.test.ts` passed\n",
        "branch": "fix/find-tool-stream-errors",
        "head_sha": "0742f811efea16861ea681838dd9a3fa617a0541",
